assistant: Subject: Read unit_amount when vendor omits price
Vendor API version 2026-10-01 renamed the product field `price` to `unit_amount`. The units didn't change: p-1001 is 1199 in both the v1 fixture and the recorded v2 response. `get_product` only read `p.price`, so on v2 responses it fell back to `null`. It now uses `p.price ?? p.unit_amount ?? null`. I made the same change in `search_products`, which reads `price` the same way. I haven't seen a v2 search response, so that part is a guess: the field there could be named differently. v1 responses still have `price`, so the v1 output is unchanged. `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint` and `pnpm test` all pass, but no test uses a v2 response, so the new path is only checked against the recorded response in the alert.

